(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Object-Oriented Programming Paradigm in Python. Detail Classes, Instance Objects, the __init__ Initializer, and the 'self' Reference Parameter with Memory Models.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations of OOP in Python:) Tj
T*
(   Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) is a software design paradigm structured around 'objects') Tj
T*
(   containing data \(attributes/state\) and code \(methods/behavior\).) Tj
T*
(   Core Pillars:) Tj
T*
(   - Class: A user-defined prototype or blueprint defining attributes and behaviors common to all) Tj
T*
(   objects of that type.) Tj
T*
(   - Instance Object: A concrete realization of a class allocated on the heap possessing unique) Tj
T*
(   state.) Tj
T*
(   - The __init__\(\) Method: An initialization hook called automatically immediately after the new) Tj
T*
(   object instance is allocated by __new__\(\). It populates instance attributes on self.) Tj
T*
(   - The self Parameter: An explicit reference to the instance upon which a method was invoked. In) Tj
T*
(   Python, obj.method\(arg\) is syntactic sugar for ClassName.method\(obj, arg\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Memory Model & Instantiation Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   When p1 = Person\('Aarav', 21\) executes:) Tj
T*
(   1. PVM calls Person.__new__\(Person, 'Aarav', 21\) -> Allocates a new PyObject on heap with) Tj
T*
(   ob_type pointing to Person class.) Tj
T*
(   2. PVM calls Person.__init__\(p1, 'Aarav', 21\) -> self is bound to the new heap address.) Tj
T*
(   3. self.name and self.age are stored as key-value pairs inside p1.__dict__.) Tj
T*
(   4. Pointer p1 is bound in caller's local scope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class Person:) Tj
T*
(   """Blueprint representing an individual.""") Tj
T*
(   # Class attribute shared across all instances) Tj
T*
(   species = "Homo sapiens") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, name: str, age: int\):) Tj
T*
(   # Instance attributes stored in instance __dict__) Tj
T*
(   self.name = name) Tj
T*
(   self.age = age) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def celebrate_birthday\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   """Instance method modifying internal state via self.""") Tj
T*
(   self.age += 1) Tj
T*
(   return f"Happy {self.age}th Birthday, {self.name}!") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   p1 = Person\("Aarav", 20\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"p1 Name: {p1.name} | Age: {p1.age} | Species: {p1.species}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(p1.celebrate_birthday\(\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Explicit desugared call) Tj
T*
(   msg = Person.celebrate_birthday\(p1\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Desugared Call Result: {msg}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Instance __dict__: {p1.__dict__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Class __dict__ Keys: {[k for k in Person.__dict__.keys\(\) if not k.startswith\('__'\)]}"\)) Tj
T*
ET

