() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Instantiation Time Complexity: O\(1\) attribute assignments.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(K\) where K is number of instance attributes in __dict__.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Class Attributes versus Instance Attributes in Python. Detail attribute shadowing, mutable class attribute bugs, and namespace lookup order.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Class Attributes vs Instance Attributes:) Tj
T*
(   - Class Attributes: Defined directly inside the class suite \(outside any method\). They are) Tj
T*
(   stored inside Class.__dict__ and shared by all instances of the class. Ideal for constants,) Tj
T*
(   configuration defaults, and instance counters.) Tj
T*
(   - Instance Attributes: Bound to self \(usually inside __init__\). Stored inside) Tj
T*
(   instance.__dict__. Each instance maintains its own independent copy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Attribute Lookup Hierarchy \(The Shadowing Trap\):) Tj
T*
(   When obj.attr is evaluated:) Tj
T*
(   1. Python checks obj.__dict__ \(Instance namespace\).) Tj
T*
(   2. If absent, Python checks Class.__dict__ and its MRO inheritance tree \(Class namespace\).) Tj
T*
(   3. If absent, calls __getattr__.) Tj
T*
(   The Shadowing Trap: Executing obj.attr = new_val assigns to the instance namespace) Tj
T*
(   \(obj.__dict__['attr'] = new_val\). It shadows \(masks\) the class attribute for that instance) Tj
T*
(   without altering the class attribute for any other instance!) Tj
T*
(   Mutable Trap: Calling obj.shared_list.append\(x\) does NOT rebind; it mutates the shared heap) Tj
T*
(   object directly, affecting all instances!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   class Employee:) Tj
T*
(   # Class attribute) Tj
T*
(   annual_bonus_pct = 0.10) Tj
T*
(   team_members = [] # Dangerous mutable class attribute!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, name: str, salary: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.name = name) Tj
T*
(   self.salary = salary) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstrating Attribute Shadowing) Tj
T*
(   e1 = Employee\("Aarav", 80_000.0\)) Tj
T*
(   e2 = Employee\("Priya", 90_000.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\("Initial Class Bonus:", Employee.annual_bonus_pct\)) Tj
T*
(   e1.annual_bonus_pct = 0.20 # Shadows class attribute ONLY for e1!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"e1 Bonus: {e1.annual_bonus_pct} \(Shadowed in e1.__dict__\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"e2 Bonus: {e2.annual_bonus_pct} \(Inherits Class Attribute\)"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Class Bonus: {Employee.annual_bonus_pct}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstrating Mutable Class Attribute Contamination) Tj
T*
(   e1.team_members.append\("Aarav"\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"e2 sees team members: {e2.team_members} \(Shared State Bug!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
ET

