12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Data Hiding and Encapsulation in Python: Public, Protected \(_var\), and Private \(__var\) attributes with Name Mangling and the @property Decorator.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Encapsulation:) Tj
T*
(   Encapsulation bundles data \(attributes\) and methods that manipulate that data into a single) Tj
T*
(   cohesive unit, restricting direct outside access to prevent unintended corruption.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python's Encapsulation Conventions:) Tj
T*
(   - Public: Standard identifier \(self.balance\). Freely accessible from any scope.) Tj
T*
(   - Protected \(Single Underscore _var\): A convention signaling to developers that the attribute) Tj
T*
(   is internal to the module or class hierarchy. Python does not enforce access restrictions.) Tj
T*
(   - Private \(Double Underscore __var\): Triggers Name Mangling. Python's compiler transforms __var) Tj
T*
(   into _ClassName__var in the class's symbol table, preventing accidental name collisions in) Tj
T*
(   subclasses.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Managed Attributes via @property:) Tj
T*
(   The @property decorator allows defining methods that can be accessed like attributes) Tj
T*
(   \(obj.balance instead of obj.get_balance\(\)\), enabling validation and computed attributes with) Tj
T*
(   zero breaking API changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   class BankAccount:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, owner: str, initial_balance: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.owner = owner) Tj
T*
(   self._account_tier = "Standard" # Protected) Tj
T*
(   self.__balance = float\(initial_balance\) # Private \(Mangled\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @property) Tj
T*
(   def balance\(self\) -> float:) Tj
T*
(   """Getter method for managed attribute.""") Tj
T*
(   return self.__balance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   @balance.setter) Tj
T*
(   def balance\(self, new_balance: float\):) Tj
T*
(   """Setter method enforcing business logic validation.""") Tj
T*
(   if new_balance < 0:) Tj
T*
(   raise ValueError\("Accounting Error: Balance cannot be negative."\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
