(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Multiple Inheritance, the Diamond Problem, and the C3 Linearization Algorithm \(MRO\) in Python with comprehensive structural traces.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Diamond Problem in Multiple Inheritance:) Tj
T*
(   Consider class D inheriting from classes B and C, both of which inherit from class A:) Tj
T*
(   A) Tj
T*
(   / \\) Tj
T*
(   B C) Tj
T*
(   \\ /) Tj
T*
(   D) Tj
T*
(   If classes B and C both override a method from A, which method should D inherit?) Tj
T*
(   In older languages \(like C++\), this creates severe ambiguity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python's Solution: The C3 Linearization Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   Since Python 2.3, Python employs the C3 Linearization Algorithm to compute a deterministic,) Tj
T*
(   monotonic Method Resolution Order \(MRO\):) Tj
T*
(   Properties of C3:) Tj
T*
ET

