(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Operator Overloading in Python. Detail Arithmetic \(__add__, __mul__\), Relational \(__eq__, __lt__\), and String Representation \(__str__, __repr__\) magic methods.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of Operator Overloading:) Tj
T*
(   Operator Overloading enables user-defined objects to interact with standard Python operators) Tj
T*
(   \(+, -, *, ==, <, etc.\) using idiomatic mathematical syntax:) Tj
T*
(   When Python evaluates a + b:) Tj
T*
(   1. Calls type\(a\).__add__\(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   2. If NotImplemented is returned, calls type\(b\).__radd__\(b, a\).) Tj
T*
(   3. If still unsupported, raises TypeError.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Distinction Between __str__ and __repr__:) Tj
T*
(   - __repr__\(self\): Unambiguous representation primarily for developers and debugging. Should) Tj
T*
(   ideally look like valid Python code to recreate the object \(e.g. ComplexNumber\(3, 4\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - __str__\(self\): Informal, readable representation formatted for end users \(e.g. 3 + 4i\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation \(Complex Number Class\):) Tj
T*
(   class ComplexNumber:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, real: float, imag: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.real = float\(real\)) Tj
T*
(   self.imag = float\(imag\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __repr__\(self\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   return f"ComplexNumber\({self.real}, {self.imag}\)") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __str__\(self\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   op = "+" if self.imag >= 0 else "-") Tj
T*
(   return f"\({self.real} {op} {abs\(self.imag\)}j\)") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __add__\(self, other\) -> 'ComplexNumber':) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(other, \(int, float\)\):) Tj
T*
(   return ComplexNumber\(self.real + other, self.imag\)) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(other, ComplexNumber\):) Tj
T*
(   return ComplexNumber\(self.real + other.real, self.imag + other.imag\)) Tj
T*
(   return NotImplemented) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __radd__\(self, other\) -> 'ComplexNumber':) Tj
T*
(   return self.__add__\(other\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __mul__\(self, other\) -> 'ComplexNumber':) Tj
T*
(   # \(a + bj\)*\(c + dj\) = \(ac - bd\) + \(ad + bc\)j) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(other, ComplexNumber\):) Tj
T*
(   r = \(self.real * other.real\) - \(self.imag * other.imag\)) Tj
T*
(   i = \(self.real * other.imag\) + \(self.imag * other.real\)) Tj
T*
(   return ComplexNumber\(r, i\)) Tj
T*
(   return NotImplemented) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __eq__\(self, other\) -> bool:) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(other, ComplexNumber\):) Tj
T*
(   return self.real == other.real and self.imag == other.imag) Tj
T*
(   return False) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   z1 = ComplexNumber\(3, 4\)) Tj
T*
(   z2 = ComplexNumber\(1, -2\)) Tj
T*
ET

