(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Container Protocol and Sequence Emulation in Python: __len__, __getitem__, __setitem__, __delitem__, __contains__, and __iter__.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Python's Container Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   By implementing specific dunder methods, a custom class can emulate Python's built-in sequences) Tj
T*
(   \(like list or dict\), supporting indexing, slicing, iteration, length queries, and membership) Tj
T*
(   tests:) Tj
T*
(   - __len__\(self\): Called by len\(\). Must return an integer >= 0.) Tj
T*
(   - __getitem__\(self, key\): Handles indexing \(obj[i]\) and slicing \(obj[a:b]\).) Tj
T*
(   - __setitem__\(self, key, val\): Handles item assignment \(obj[i] = val\).) Tj
T*
(   - __delitem__\(self, key\): Handles item deletion \(del obj[i]\).) Tj
T*
(   - __contains__\(self, item\): Handles membership test \(item in obj\).) Tj
T*
(   - __iter__\(self\): Handles for-in loops and iter\(obj\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation \(Bounded Custom Circular Buffer\):) Tj
T*
(   class CircularBuffer:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, capacity: int\):) Tj
T*
(   self._cap = capacity) Tj
T*
(   self._items = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def append\(self, item\):) Tj
T*
(   if len\(self._items\) == self._cap:) Tj
T*
(   self._items.pop\(0\) # Drop oldest) Tj
T*
(   self._items.append\(item\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __len__\(self\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   return len\(self._items\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __getitem__\(self, index\):) Tj
T*
(   return self._items[index]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __setitem__\(self, index, value\):) Tj
T*
(   self._items[index] = value) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __contains__\(self, value\) -> bool:) Tj
T*
(   return value in self._items) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __iter__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   return iter\(self._items\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

