(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Abstract Base Classes \(ABCs\) in Python. Detail the abc module, @abstractmethod decorator, interface enforcement, and virtual subclass registration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Abstract Base Classes:) Tj
T*
(   In software architecture, an Abstract Base Class \(ABC\) defines an interface contract specifying) Tj
T*
(   methods and properties that all concrete derived classes MUST implement:) Tj
T*
(   - Cannot be instantiated directly.) Tj
T*
(   - Derived classes that fail to override all @abstractmethod declarations will fail) Tj
T*
(   instantiation at runtime with a TypeError.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Virtual Subclass Registration:) Tj
T*
(   ABCs in Python support 'Virtual Subclasses' via ABC.register\(ConcreteClass\).) Tj
T*
(   A virtual subclass is recognized by isinstance\(obj, ABC\) and issubclass\(Concrete, ABC\) as) Tj
T*
(   adhering to the contract without needing to inherit directly from the ABC class hierarchy!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   from abc import ABC, abstractmethod) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class PaymentGateway\(ABC\):) Tj
T*
(   """Abstract base class defining payment interface contract.""") Tj
T*
ET

