(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Descriptor Protocol in Python \(__get__, __set__, __delete__\). Implement a TypeChecked and BoundedNumeric descriptor for model validation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Descriptors:) Tj
T*
(   A Descriptor is an object attribute whose access lifecycle is controlled by implementing one or) Tj
T*
(   more of the descriptor protocol methods:) Tj
T*
(   - __get__\(self, instance, owner\): Invoked on attribute read \(obj.attr\).) Tj
T*
(   - __set__\(self, instance, value\): Invoked on attribute write \(obj.attr = val\).) Tj
T*
(   - __delete__\(self, instance\): Invoked on attribute deletion \(del obj.attr\).) Tj
T*
(   Descriptors are the underlying engine behind @property, @classmethod, @staticmethod, and modern) Tj
T*
(   ORM libraries \(SQLAlchemy, Django Models\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class BoundedFloat:) Tj
T*
(   """Data descriptor validating float range.""") Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, min_val: float, max_val: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.min_val = min_val) Tj
T*
(   self.max_val = max_val) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __set_name__\(self, owner, name\):) Tj
T*
(   self.storage_name = f"_{name}") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __get__\(self, instance, owner\):) Tj
T*
(   if instance is None:) Tj
T*
(   return self) Tj
T*
(   return getattr\(instance, self.storage_name, None\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __set__\(self, instance, value\):) Tj
T*
(   if not isinstance\(value, \(int, float\)\):) Tj
T*
(   raise TypeError\(f"Attribute '{self.storage_name[1:]}' must be a numeric float."\)) Tj
T*
(   if not \(self.min_val <= value <= self.max_val\):) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
