(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Mixin Classes and Cooperative Multiple Inheritance in Python. Implement a JSONSerializable and LoggingMixin system.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of Mixin Classes:) Tj
T*
(   A Mixin is a specialized class providing reusable behavioral methods intended to be mixed into) Tj
T*
(   multiple, otherwise unrelated classes through multiple inheritance.) Tj
T*
(   Guidelines for Mixins:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mixins should NOT be instantiated standalone.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mixins should NOT maintain extensive independent state \(rarely define a separate __init__\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Facilitates modular code composition over deep rigid inheritance hierarchies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   import json) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class JSONSerializableMixin:) Tj
T*
(   """Mixin providing automatic JSON serialization.""") Tj
T*
(   def to_json\(self\) -> str:) Tj
T*
(   return json.dumps\(self.__dict__, default=str, indent=2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class AuditLoggingMixin:) Tj
T*
(   """Mixin logging state changes.""") Tj
T*
(   def log_event\(self, action: str\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[AUDIT] {self.__class__.__name__} performed '{action}' at ID {id\(self\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
