(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a State Machine Pattern in Python using OOP: OrderState, PendingState, PaidState, ShippedState, and DeliveredState.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of the State Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   The State Pattern allows an object to alter its behavior when its internal state changes. The) Tj
T*
(   object will appear to change its class:) Tj
T*
(   - Context: Order) Tj
T*
(   - State Interface: OrderState) Tj
T*
(   - Concrete States: PendingState -> PaidState -> ShippedState -> DeliveredState.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   from abc import ABC, abstractmethod) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class OrderContext:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, order_id: str\):) Tj
T*
(   self.order_id = order_id) Tj
T*
(   self._state = PendingState\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def set_state\(self, state: 'OrderState'\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[{self.order_id}] State Transition: {self._state.__class__.__name__} ->) Tj
T*
(   {state.__class__.__name__}"\)) Tj
T*
(   self._state = state) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def pay\(self\): self._state.pay\(self\)) Tj
T*
(   def ship\(self\): self._state.ship\(self\)) Tj
T*
(   def deliver\(self\): self._state.deliver\(self\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class OrderState\(ABC\):) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
(   def pay\(self, ctx: OrderContext\): pass) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
(   def ship\(self, ctx: OrderContext\): pass) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
ET

