12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the @dataclass Decorator \(PEP 557\) in Python. Contrast dataclasses with standard classes, namedtuples, and pydantic models.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Motivation for Dataclasses:) Tj
T*
(   In standard Python, writing data-centric classes involves tedious, boilerplate code: writing) Tj
T*
(   __init__, __repr__, __eq__, __hash__, and comparison methods manually.) Tj
T*
(   Codified in PEP 557 \(Python 3.7+\), @dataclass automatically generates these special methods by) Tj
T*
(   inspecting class variable type annotations!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Feature Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   - Standard Class: Maximum flexibility, high boilerplate code.) Tj
T*
(   - namedtuple: Memory-efficient, immutable, indexable tuple subclass.) Tj
T*
(   - Dataclass: Full class identity, mutable or frozen \(frozen=True\), default values, field) Tj
T*
(   factories.) Tj
T*
(   - Pydantic: Dataclass-like syntax with runtime data parsing and strict schema validation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   from dataclasses import dataclass, field) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
