(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Custom Iterator and Iterable Class in Python: FibonacciIterable supporting the Iterator Protocol \(__iter__ and __next__\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Mechanics of the Iterator Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   An object is Iterable if it implements __iter__\(\) returning an Iterator.) Tj
T*
(   An object is an Iterator if it implements:) Tj
T*
(   1. __iter__\(\): Returns self.) Tj
T*
(   2. __next__\(\): Returns the next item in the sequence; raises StopIteration when iteration) Tj
T*
(   completes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class FibonacciIterable:) Tj
T*
(   """Custom iterable sequence generating Fibonacci numbers up to limit.""") Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, limit: int\):) Tj
T*
(   self.limit = limit) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __iter__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   """Returns a fresh iterator instance.""") Tj
T*
(   return FibonacciIterator\(self.limit\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class FibonacciIterator:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, limit: int\):) Tj
T*
ET

