(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Dependency Injection Container in Python using Classes and Reflection for service registration and resolution.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis:) Tj
T*
(   Dependency Injection \(DI\) is a software design pattern where an object's dependencies are) Tj
T*
(   injected by an external assembler rather than created internally, decoupling components and) Tj
T*
(   enabling testing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class DIContainer:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   self._services = {}) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def register_singleton\(self, service_type, instance\):) Tj
T*
(   self._services[service_type] = instance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def resolve\(self, service_type\):) Tj
T*
(   if service_type not in self._services:) Tj
T*
(   raise KeyError\(f"Service {service_type.__name__} not registered."\)) Tj
T*
(   return self._services[service_type]) Tj
T*
ET

