12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Custom Context Manager in Python using OOP: DatabaseConnectionManager implementing __enter__ and __exit__ with exception handling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mechanics of Context Managers:) Tj
T*
(   A context manager controls resource setup and teardown via the with statement:) Tj
T*
(   - __enter__\(\): Prepares resource and returns target object.) Tj
T*
(   - __exit__\(exc_type, exc_val, exc_tb\): Executes teardown \(closing connections, releasing) Tj
T*
(   locks\). Returning True suppresses caught exceptions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class DatabaseTransaction:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, db_name: str\):) Tj
T*
(   self.db = db_name) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __enter__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[TX START] Connected to {self.db}. Began transaction."\)) Tj
T*
(   return self) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def query\(self, sql: str\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" Executing: {sql}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __exit__\(self, exc_type, exc_val, exc_tb\):) Tj
T*
(   if exc_type is not None:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[TX ROLLBACK] Error occurred: {exc_val}. Changes rolled back!"\)) Tj
T*
(   return False # Propagate exception) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
