(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an Object Relational Mapping \(ORM\) Style Active Record Entity in Python using Metaclasses and Field descriptors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Active Record ORM:) Tj
T*
(   An Active Record entity maps a database table to a Python class, and individual rows to) Tj
T*
(   instances of that class. Fields are validated using descriptors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class Field:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, data_type\):) Tj
T*
(   self.data_type = data_type) Tj
T*
(   def __set_name__\(self, owner, name\):) Tj
T*
(   self.name = name) Tj
T*
(   def __get__\(self, instance, owner\):) Tj
T*
(   if instance is None: return self) Tj
T*
(   return instance.__dict__.get\(self.name\)) Tj
T*
(   def __set__\(self, instance, value\):) Tj
T*
(   if not isinstance\(value, self.data_type\):) Tj
T*
(   raise TypeError\(f"Field '{self.name}' must be of type {self.data_type.__name__}."\)) Tj
T*
(   instance.__dict__[self.name] = value) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class UserRecord:) Tj
T*
(   id = Field\(int\)) Tj
T*
(   username = Field\(str\)) Tj
T*
(   email = Field\(str\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, id: int, username: str, email: str\):) Tj
T*
(   self.id = id) Tj
T*
(   self.username = username) Tj
T*
(   self.email = email) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def save\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Saving User #{self.id} \('{self.username}'\) to database."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   user = UserRecord\(101, "aarav", "aarav@cse.edu"\)) Tj
T*
(   user.save\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   user.id = "invalid_id") Tj
T*
(   except TypeError as ex:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
