(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Strategy Design Pattern in Python using Classes: PaymentProcessor with CreditCardStrategy, PayPalStrategy, and CryptoStrategy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of Strategy Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   The Strategy pattern defines a family of algorithms, encapsulates each one, and makes them) Tj
T*
(   interchangeable, allowing the algorithm to vary independently from clients that use it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   from abc import ABC, abstractmethod) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class PaymentStrategy\(ABC\):) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
(   def pay\(self, amount: float\): pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class CreditCardStrategy\(PaymentStrategy\):) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, card_num: str\): self.card_num = card_num) Tj
T*
(   def pay\(self, amount: float\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Paid ${amount:.2f} using Credit Card ending in {self.card_num[-4:]}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class CryptoStrategy\(PaymentStrategy\):) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, wallet_addr: str\): self.wallet = wallet_addr) Tj
T*
(   def pay\(self, amount: float\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Paid ${amount:.2f} using Ethereum Wallet: {self.wallet[:8]}..."\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class ShoppingCart:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, strategy: PaymentStrategy\):) Tj
T*
(   self.strategy = strategy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def checkout\(self, total: float\):) Tj
T*
(   self.strategy.pay\(total\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   cart1 = ShoppingCart\(CreditCardStrategy\("4111222233334444"\)\)) Tj
T*
(   cart1.checkout\(150.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   cart2 = ShoppingCart\(CryptoStrategy\("0x71C...B29"\)\)) Tj
T*
(   cart2.checkout\(300.0\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(1\) strategy invocation.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) strategy object.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
