(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Exception Hierarchies:) Tj
T*
(   User-defined exceptions should inherit from Python's built-in Exception class \(never) Tj
T*
(   BaseException\).) Tj
T*
(   Structuring exceptions in a domain hierarchy allows callers to catch broad categories of errors) Tj
T*
(   or handle fine-grained failures individually.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class ECommerceError\(Exception\):) Tj
T*
(   """Base exception for all domain errors.""") Tj
T*
(   pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class InventoryError\(ECommerceError\):) Tj
T*
(   """Errors related to stock availability.""") Tj
T*
(   pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class OutOfStockError\(InventoryError\):) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, sku: str, requested: int, available: int\):) Tj
T*
(   super\(\).__init__\(f"SKU {sku} is out of stock. Requested: {requested}, Available: {available}"\)) Tj
T*
(   self.sku = sku) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class PaymentError\(ECommerceError\):) Tj
T*
(   """Errors related to transaction processing.""") Tj
T*
(   pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Demonstration) Tj
T*
(   def order_product\(sku: str, qty: int, stock: int\):) Tj
T*
(   if qty > stock:) Tj
T*
(   raise OutOfStockError\(sku, qty, stock\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Order placed for {qty} units of {sku}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   order_product\("SKU-100", 5, 2\)) Tj
T*
(   except OutOfStockError as err:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Caught Specific OutOfStockError: {err}"\)) Tj
T*
(   except ECommerceError as err:) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Caught Broad Domain Error: {err}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Exception Instantiation Time: O\(1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(Depth\) traceback frames.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
