/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Metaclasses in Python in depth. Implement a ModelValidatorMeta metaclass that validates that all subclass attributes have docstrings.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Metaclasses:) Tj
T*
(   In Python, classes are themselves instances of metaclasses. The default metaclass is type:) Tj
T*
(   type\(name, bases, dict\)) Tj
T*
(   A custom metaclass intercepts class construction before the class object is created in memory,) Tj
T*
(   enabling automated schema enforcement and attribute validation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class DocumentedClassMeta\(type\):) Tj
T*
(   def __new__\(mcls, name, bases, attrs\):) Tj
T*
(   # Enforce that every concrete subclass has a docstring) Tj
T*
(   if not attrs.get\('__doc__'\):) Tj
T*
(   raise TypeError\(f"Architecture Violation: Class '{name}' must have a docstring!"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return super\(\).__new__\(mcls, name, bases, attrs\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

