(   [Problem Statement]: Implement the Command Design Pattern in Python with Undo/Redo Capability using Classes and Command Stacks.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Principles of Command Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   Encapsulates a request as an object, thereby letting you parameterize clients with different) Tj
T*
(   requests, queue or log requests, and support undoable operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   from abc import ABC, abstractmethod) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class ICommand\(ABC\):) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
(   def execute\(self\): pass) Tj
T*
(   @abstractmethod) Tj
T*
(   def undo\(self\): pass) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class TextDocument:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self\): self.text = "") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class AppendTextCommand\(ICommand\):) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self, doc: TextDocument, text_to_append: str\):) Tj
T*
(   self.doc = doc) Tj
T*
(   self.text_to_append = text_to_append) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def execute\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   self.doc.text += self.text_to_append) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def undo\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   self.doc.text = self.doc.text[:-len\(self.text_to_append\)]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   class EditorInvoker:) Tj
T*
(   def __init__\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   self._undo_stack = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def execute_command\(self, cmd: ICommand\):) Tj
T*
(   cmd.execute\(\)) Tj
T*
(   self._undo_stack.append\(cmd\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def undo\(self\):) Tj
T*
(   if self._undo_stack:) Tj
T*
(   cmd = self._undo_stack.pop\(\)) Tj
T*
(   cmd.undo\(\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
ET

